course: dictionary
lesson: 13465
title: A hundredfold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hundredfold means a hundred times as much or as many. Break it into two parts: hundred, and fold, which means times, as in twofold or threefold.
explain: In maths, if you grow 5 a hundredfold, you multiply it by 100 and get 500. «The number of bacteria grew a hundredfold in one day.» That means it became 100 times bigger. Check by swapping in "100 times as much": if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Writers also use hundredfold to mean "greatly, many times over", without counting exactly. In the Bible, a sower's seed «produced a hundredfold», meaning a huge harvest. Context tells you whether the number is exact or just a way of saying "a very great amount".
fact: Hundredfold means a hundred times as much or as many.
fact: Hundredfold can be an adverb («The price rose a hundredfold») or an adjective («a hundredfold increase»).
fact: "Fold" means times, so twofold means two times and tenfold means ten times.
fact: «Prices rose a hundredfold» means the prices became 100 times higher.
fact: In the Bible parable of the sower, «a hundredfold» means a huge harvest, many times over.
exercise: «The small plant grew a hundredfold in one summer.» What does hundredfold mean? | Only a little bit more | Less than before | *A hundred times as much | Ten times as much
exercise: If the number 5 grows a hundredfold, what is the new number? | 50 | *500 | 105 | 5,000
exercise: Which word means ten times as much? | tenner | tenth | tens | *tenfold
test: «Prices rose a hundredfold after the storm.» What does this mean? | Prices fell to nothing | Prices stayed exactly the same | *Prices became 100 times higher | Prices rose by one penny
test: «The farmer's harvest was a hundredfold.» What does this suggest? | Exactly one hundred apples | *A huge amount, many times over | A very small harvest | A harvest that was late
exam: If a team's score grows a hundredfold from 4 points, what is the new score? | 40 | 4,000 | 104 | *400
